---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import V from '../components/V.astro';
import { business } from '../data/site';
---

<Base title="Privacy notice | Route 66 Driving School" description="How Route 66 Driving School uses your personal information.">
  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap prose">
      <p class="eyebrow">Privacy</p>
      <h1>Privacy notice</h1>
      <p>Last updated: 3 October 2026.</p>

      <h2>Who we are</h2>
      <p>
        {business.name} is run by <V v={business.owner} />, a {business.legalForm}, who is the data controller for the
        information described here. Address: <V v={business.address} />. Email:
        <a href={`mailto:${business.email}`}><V v={business.email} /></a>.
      </p>

      <h2>What we collect and why</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>When you contact us</strong> by WhatsApp, phone or email: your name, phone number and anything you
          tell us, such as your area and availability. We use this to reply and to arrange lessons (taking steps at your
          request before a contract).
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>When you book lessons</strong>: your address for pick-up, provisional licence details, lesson and test
          dates, and payment records. We need this to provide lessons and meet our legal and insurance obligations.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Website statistics</strong>: if enabled, we use cookie-free analytics that count visits and clicks on
          our contact buttons without identifying you or storing anything on your device. This helps us improve the site.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>WhatsApp</h2>
      <p>
        Our WhatsApp buttons are plain links. Nothing from WhatsApp loads on this website. If you message us, WhatsApp
        (Meta) processes your messages under its own privacy policy.
      </p>

      <h2>Cookies</h2>
      <p>This website does not set cookies.</p>

      <h2>Who we share it with</h2>
      <p>
        We do not sell your information. We use a small number of service providers to run this website and our email
        (for example our web host). We may share details with DVSA when booking or managing driving tests, or where the
        law requires it.
      </p>

      <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
      <p>
        Enquiries that do not lead to lessons are deleted within 12 months. Pupil records are kept for up to 6 years
        after your last lesson for accounting and insurance purposes.
      </p>

      <h2>Your rights</h2>
      <p>
        You can ask to see, correct or delete your information, or object to how we use it. Contact us using the details
        above. If you are unhappy with how we handle your data, you can complain to the Information Commissioner's Office
        at <a href="https://ico.org.uk/make-a-complaint/">ico.org.uk</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
